# --- Remote power-cycle escape valve (Pass 7 Track B) -----
#
# Optional. When KASA_DEVICE_IP is set, dead-man's heartbeat uses the TP-Link
# Kasa smart plug to power-cycle the Skytech tower after 3 failed auto-restart
# attempts in 24h (the 4th-attempt escape valve). When unset, behavior is
# unchanged: Discord CRITICAL fires with "hold the power button for 5 seconds"
# as the terminal operator action.
#
# Setup:
#   1. Purchase a TP-Link Kasa HS103/HS105/HS110 smart plug ($10-20).
#   2. Plug the Skytech tower into it.
#   3. Connect the plug to your home Wi-Fi via the Kasa app.
#   4. Assign a STATIC IP to the plug in your router's DHCP reservation table
#      (so the IP never changes while you're on vacation).
#   5. Set the three vars below.
#
# Note: ALL THREE vars must be set together. If only some are set, startup-
# config-check.ts will warn at boot (partial config is worse than none because
# it creates a false impression that the escape valve is active).
#
KASA_DEVICE_IP=        # IPv4 of the smart plug (e.g. 192.168.1.42)
KASA_USERNAME=         # Kasa cloud account email (used only for auth if needed)
KASA_PASSWORD=         # Kasa cloud account password

